## \uc0\u55356 \u57263  Feature Testing Guide\
\
### 1. \uc0\u9989  Account Deletion (NEW - Addresses Rejection Issue)\
\
**Location:** Profile \uc0\u8594  Settings \u8594  Delete Account\
\
**Steps to Test:**\
1. Register or login with an account (NOT anonymous)\
2. Tap **hamburger menu** (\uc0\u8801 ) \u8594  **Profile**\
3. Scroll down to **Settings** section\
4. Tap **"Delete Account"** (red text at bottom)\
5. Review data counts shown in dialog\
6. Type **"DELETE"** in capital letters\
7. Enter your password to confirm\
8. Account and all data permanently deleted\
9. Redirected to login screen\
\
**What to Verify:**\
- Dialog shows count of user's data (evidence, documents, etc.)\
- Requires typing "DELETE" exactly\
- Requires password verification for registered users\
- Anonymous users can also delete all their data (no password required)\
- All user data removed after deletion\
\
---\
\
### 2. \uc0\u55356 \u57252  Live Audio Support Groups (Addresses Discoverability Issue)\
\
**Location:** Home \uc0\u8594  Community Tab \u8594  Support Groups\
\
**Steps to Test:**\
1. Login or use anonymous access\
2. Tap **"Community"** tab in bottom navigation\
3. Tap **"Support Groups"** tab at top\
4. You'll see:\
   - **"Browse Groups"** button - View available groups\
   - **"Create Group"** button - Start your own support group\
   - List of active groups (if any exist)\
\
**To Create a Live Audio Group:**\
1. Tap **"Create Group"** button\
2. Fill in details:\
   - **Group Name:** e.g., "Evening Support Circle"\
   - **Description:** Brief description\
   - **Type:** Select "Audio Call" for live audio groups\
   - **Privacy:** Public or Private\
   - **Max Members:** Choose capacity\
3. Tap **"Create Group"**\
4. Group appears in the list\
\
**To Join a Live Audio Group:**\
1. Tap on any group in the list\
2. Tap **"Join Group"** button\
3. If it's a live audio session:\
   - Microphone permission requested\
   - Can unmute to speak\
   - Can listen to others\
4. Tap **"Leave"** to exit\
\
**Technical Details:**\
- Uses Agora RTC Engine for real-time audio\
- No video - audio only for privacy\
- All audio sessions are encrypted\
- No recordings stored\
\
---\
\
